      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s first public library opened in 1939 and joined the Nantahala Regional Library system the following year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robbinsville%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original Graham County Courthouse, built in 1874, collapsed during a murder trial, prompting a wooden replacement in 1895 that was the last wooden courthouse in North Carolina.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robbinsville%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Fontana Dam, the tallest dam east of the Rockies, was constructed in the 1940s to supply hydroelectric power for World War II.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
